        "definition": "The two mandatory semantic components of any complete thought: Focus (whom or what the sentence is about) and Information (what is said or done about the focus).",
        "textbook_citation": "God's Gift of Language B, Page 2 & Video Manual Page 3",
        "exact_textbook_quote": "Every sentence has two parts: what the sentence is about (the focus), and what is happening or what is said about it.",
